WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.087
He likes to pass the ball more
when he drives with his left.

00:00:04.087 --> 00:00:07.048
And I'd prefer him to pass
than to shoot or score.

00:00:14.014 --> 00:00:14.889
 
What's up guys,

00:00:14.889 --> 00:00:15.807
 
Jrue Holiday here.

00:00:15.807 --> 00:00:16.850
I'm going to take you

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:17.934
guys through my film session.

00:00:17.934 --> 00:00:19.352
The break down.

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:22.439
Just to show you guys what
I do on a day-to-day basis

00:00:22.439 --> 00:00:24.315
against the best
players in the world.

00:00:24.315 --> 00:00:26.359
And why I'm the best
defender in the league.

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:27.068
Let's go.

00:00:27.068 --> 00:00:31.031
What's hard about Steph
is he's super quick.

00:00:31.031 --> 00:00:32.782
He's really quick,
really shifty.

00:00:32.782 --> 00:00:35.118
We know how he can
get that shot off you.

00:00:35.118 --> 00:00:37.704
So this, again
for me, it kind of

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:40.373
becomes like a long
distance track meet.

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:42.792
Where one of us are
going to get tired,

00:00:42.792 --> 00:00:44.210
and it's not going
to be me first.

00:00:47.255 --> 00:00:50.216
 
We already know that I'm staying
with Steph no matter what.

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:53.303
I get hit by a screen,
fight through the screen.

00:00:53.303 --> 00:00:56.389
Over the top, underneath, but
most of the time over the top.

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:59.476
Because I can stay closer
to him and possibly

00:00:59.476 --> 00:01:01.311
run him off the 3-point line.

00:01:01.311 --> 00:01:03.938
At this point, I'm
just attached to him.

00:01:03.938 --> 00:01:04.939
I'm stronger than him.

00:01:04.939 --> 00:01:07.984
So I feel like I just try
to be physical with him.

00:01:07.984 --> 00:01:12.739
And I don't want to give them
any room to get comfortable.

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:14.949
Don't let him just go
whichever way he wants to go.

00:01:14.949 --> 00:01:17.452
And as they're doing
that dribble handoff,

00:01:17.452 --> 00:01:18.870
I get my hand on the ball.

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:20.872
There's also another term
that we use, is called

00:01:20.872 --> 00:01:21.831
"on an island."

00:01:21.831 --> 00:01:25.126
So if I have Steph by myself
and he's in the corner.

00:01:25.126 --> 00:01:27.253
And it's just me and him.

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:28.963
I'm "on the island" with Steph.

00:01:28.963 --> 00:01:31.049
And usually, when
you're on that island,

00:01:31.049 --> 00:01:34.260
somebody from behind you has
to communicate and tell you

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:35.345
what's going on.

00:01:35.345 --> 00:01:38.306
So I crowd him because I
don't want him to shoot 3,

00:01:38.306 --> 00:01:39.641
I don't want him give him space.

00:01:39.641 --> 00:01:42.393
And then I kind of send
him in one direction.

00:01:42.393 --> 00:01:44.145
You can see my right
foot is up at the top

00:01:44.145 --> 00:01:45.021
of that 3-point line.

00:01:45.021 --> 00:01:47.065
And I'm kind of giving
him that baseline drive,

00:01:47.065 --> 00:01:48.983
knowing that my helper
is going to be there.

00:01:48.983 --> 00:01:51.444
And then being able to
just kind of reach in

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:53.029
and knock that
ball out of bounds.

00:01:53.029 --> 00:01:54.864
I didn't know the exact metrics.

00:01:54.864 --> 00:01:57.492
But I also know for
us to win the game,

00:01:57.492 --> 00:01:59.828
he's going to have
to really fight.

00:01:59.828 --> 00:02:01.996
That's cool, that
even just here,

00:02:01.996 --> 00:02:03.915
being able to get
that on record.

00:02:03.915 --> 00:02:05.875
Just like how much you
pressure up on somebody.

00:02:05.875 --> 00:02:07.585
And these are
professional athletes.

00:02:07.585 --> 00:02:08.878
And they're best way to do it.

00:02:08.878 --> 00:02:11.172
That's why they're in the
NBA and they make this money.

00:02:11.172 --> 00:02:14.342
Dame is called "Logo
Dame" for a reason.

00:02:14.342 --> 00:02:17.053
It's not easy to guard
somebody up that high.

00:02:17.053 --> 00:02:19.430
That's where I hear a
lot of my teammates.

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:21.182
And what's going on,
if there's a screen,

00:02:21.182 --> 00:02:22.016
which way to send him.

00:02:22.016 --> 00:02:23.601
I'm already picking him
up close to half court.

00:02:23.601 --> 00:02:25.854
The screen comes up, so
they communicate the screen.

00:02:25.854 --> 00:02:29.691
I get underneath the screen
because the big man is up.

00:02:29.691 --> 00:02:33.736
Four, five, maybe even six
feet above the 3-point line,

00:02:33.736 --> 00:02:35.530
which Dame is capable
of shooting that.

00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:37.699
But I get underneath so
that he doesn't split.

00:02:37.699 --> 00:02:43.163
He doesn't try to dribble back
and split between me and him.

00:02:43.163 --> 00:02:45.206
You see I kind of cut him off.

00:02:45.206 --> 00:02:47.250
And then I keep
him at that angle.

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:48.918
So that he has one way to go.

00:02:48.918 --> 00:02:51.588
I would prefer the ball
out of Damian's hands.

00:02:51.588 --> 00:02:57.177
And you see Steph, Dame,
Trae Young, Luka, LeBron.

00:02:57.177 --> 00:02:58.887
You see these guys
shoot from half court.

00:02:58.887 --> 00:03:00.930
You see a big shot
like that go in,

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:04.976
and that could really spark
something in the score.

00:03:04.976 --> 00:03:06.811
Defense is hard.

00:03:06.811 --> 00:03:09.230
I mean like Boston,
where you have Kemba.

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:11.691
Loves to shoot the 3, but
also can get to the basket.

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:15.528
You have Jason, who is a
really good, damn near great, one-on-one player.

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:17.071
You have Jaylen Brown.

00:03:17.071 --> 00:03:19.365
So all them, I view
them differently.

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:20.783
It's corner fill.

00:03:20.783 --> 00:03:22.827
And you're not supposed
to leave corner fill.

00:03:22.827 --> 00:03:24.245
Our philosophy,
don't leave corner

00:03:24.245 --> 00:03:26.664
fill because that's one of
the best shots in the league.

00:03:26.664 --> 00:03:29.709
I mean, guys make that
with our eyes closed.

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:32.212
I ended up being
late to the close-up.

00:03:32.212 --> 00:03:34.797
Which, at this point, I'm
thinking, "I messed up.

00:03:34.797 --> 00:03:36.633
Let me try to run
him off the line."

00:03:36.633 --> 00:03:39.177
So I overshoot it.

00:03:39.177 --> 00:03:41.179
And I try to get
on his left side

00:03:41.179 --> 00:03:43.139
to try to make him
go down the line,

00:03:43.139 --> 00:03:44.766
knowing that my helper's there.

00:03:44.766 --> 00:03:47.810
Kemba to go up against somebody
like Brook, who's seven feet.

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:49.687
That's going to be
a difficult shot.

00:03:49.687 --> 00:03:52.106
Jason, I feel like
I'm quicker than him.

00:03:52.106 --> 00:03:54.442
So I usually try to
pressure up on him.

00:03:54.442 --> 00:03:57.278
For one, he probably has
three or four inches on me.

00:03:57.278 --> 00:04:00.073
He does a nice little crab
dribble to a step-back.

00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:02.116
My momentum is forward.

00:04:02.116 --> 00:04:04.369
I also know he's going to
take the step-back shot.

00:04:04.369 --> 00:04:07.205
And I'm going to just
contest the best that I can.

00:04:07.205 --> 00:04:09.457
That's kind of
where my mind goes

00:04:09.457 --> 00:04:13.378
when I try to guard guys
who are prolific scorers.

00:04:13.378 --> 00:04:15.588
To know that like you can
pressure up on somebody,

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:19.592
and still do a great job with
them is y'all just really making me feel good.

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:22.220
You know, out here, I should be
a Defensive Player of the Year.

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:24.055
Kids need to learn defense, man.

00:04:24.055 --> 00:04:25.056
It's fun.

00:04:25.056 --> 00:04:27.016
Kind of give you my
insight on defense.

00:04:27.016 --> 00:04:28.559
And what it takes.

00:04:28.559 --> 00:04:30.228
You got to start
locking people up, man.

00:04:30.228 --> 00:04:31.521
It's the way to go.

00:04:31.521 --> 00:04:32.605
Get under the skin.

00:04:32.605 --> 00:04:34.232
Stop them defensively, man.

00:04:34.232 --> 00:04:35.483
I love it.

